## SSH Keys

### Generate SSH Key

```bash
# Generate ed25519 key (recommended)
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "your@email.com"

# Or RSA (older, more compatible)
ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "your@email.com"

# Save to default location: ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
# Set passphrase (recommended)
```

### Add to SSH Agent

```bash
# Start ssh-agent (if not running)
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"

# Add key to agent
ssh-add ~/.ssh/id_ed25519

# Add with passphrase stored in keychain (macOS)
ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

### Add to GitHub

```bash
# Copy public key
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub | pbcopy

# Or display it
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

# Add to GitHub:
# Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New SSH key
# Paste the public key
```

### SSH Config

**File:** `~/.ssh/config` (safe to version control, no secrets)

```bash
# GitHub
Host github.com
  HostName github.com
  User git
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
  AddKeysToAgent yes
  UseKeychain yes

# Work server
Host work-server
  HostName server.company.com
  User your-username
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
  Port 22
```

**Permissions:**

```bash
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/config
chmod 700 ~/.ssh
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
chmod 644 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

---

## GPG Keys

### Generate GPG Key

```bash
# Generate key
gpg --full-generate-key

# Select:
# 1. RSA and RSA
# 2. 4096 bits
# 3. Key doesn't expire (or set expiration)
# 4. Your name and email

# List keys
gpg --list-secret-keys --keyid-format=long
```

### Export Public Key

```bash
# Get key ID
gpg --list-secret-keys --keyid-format=long
# sec   rsa4096/ABCD1234EFGH5678 2024-01-01

# Export public key
gpg --armor --export ABCD1234EFGH5678

# Copy to clipboard
gpg --armor --export ABCD1234EFGH5678 | pbcopy

# Add to GitHub:
# Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New GPG key
```

### Sign Git Commits

**File:** `home/jimmy/programs/git.nix`

```nix
programs.git = {
  signing = {
    key = "ABCD1234EFGH5678";
    signByDefault = true;
  };
};
```

**Then rebuild:**

```bash
nix-rebuild

# Verify
g config --list | grep gpg
```

### Backup GPG Keys

```bash
# Backup private key (KEEP SECURE!)
gpg --export-secret-keys ABCD1234EFGH5678 > ~/private-backup.gpg

# Store securely (encrypted drive, password manager, etc.)
# NEVER commit to git!
```

---

## AWS Credentials

### Credentials File

**File:** `~/.aws/credentials` (**NEVER commit!**)

```bash
# Edit credentials
code ~/.aws/credentials

# Add credentials
[personal]
aws_access_key_id = AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE
aws_secret_access_key = wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY

[work-dev]
aws_access_key_id = AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE
aws_secret_access_key = wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY
```

**Permissions:**

```bash
chmod 600 ~/.aws/credentials
chmod 600 ~/.aws/config
```

### Config File

**File:** `~/.aws/config` (safe to commit, no secrets)

```bash
# Edit config
awsconf

# Profiles with SSO (no credentials needed)
[profile work-prod]
sso_start_url = https://company.awsapps.com/start
sso_region = us-east-1
sso_account_id = 123456789012
sso_role_name = Developer
region = us-east-1

[profile personal]
region = us-east-1
output = json
```

### AWS SSO

```bash
# Login with SSO (no credentials stored)
awslogin

# Credentials are temporary tokens
# Stored in ~/.aws/sso/cache/ (auto-managed)

# Check current profile
awswho
```

### MFA Tokens

If using MFA:

```bash
# Get session token
aws sts get-session-token \
  --serial-number arn:aws:iam::123456789012:mfa/user \
  --token-code 123456

# Use temporary credentials
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID="..."
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="..."
export AWS_SESSION_TOKEN="..."
```

---

## API Keys

### Environment Variables

**File:** `~/.zsh_secrets`

```bash
# AI/ML APIs
export OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-..."
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
export HUGGINGFACE_TOKEN="hf_..."

# Cloud services
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN="..."
export VERCEL_TOKEN="..."

# Other services
export SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL="https://hooks.slack.com/..."
export NOTION_API_KEY="secret_..."
```

### Project-Specific Secrets

**File:** `~/Dev/my-project/.env` (**Add to .gitignore!**)

```bash
# In project directory
cd ~/Dev/my-project

# Create .env file
cat > .env <<EOF
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@localhost/mydb
SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key
API_KEY=abc123
EOF

# Add to .gitignore
echo ".env" >> .gitignore

# Commit .gitignore
g aa
g cm "Add .env to gitignore"
```

**Load in Python:**

```python
# Use python-dotenv
from dotenv import load_dotenv
import os

load_dotenv()
api_key = os.getenv("API_KEY")
```

### Password Managers

Consider using a password manager:

- **1Password** - CLI integration
- **Bitwarden** - CLI available
- **LastPass** - CLI available

**Example with 1Password CLI:**

```bash
# Install 1Password CLI
brew install --cask 1password-cli

# Login
op signin

# Get secret
op item get "OpenAI API Key" --fields password
```

